      ":question/problem": "![](images/e4/e4b568fe2226154be401a2332c718f143954d98fdbd8a0c679fdb99fcdd47d14.png)\n\nSarah interviewed some parents, asking them how much time their children spend playing outdoors per day. The information she received is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n- There is only one child aged $6$ among those surveyed.\n- None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors."
