      ":question/problem": "![](images/57/5768d8f90d3dd754471a69d25582eca6cdb2f4993b9b22020dc9f2038aa61954.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above summarizes data collected by a Midwestern high school showing the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the class size. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one class reported a total of $6$ absences in the month.\n- Two classes have a total of $20$ students each.\n- Only one class has more than $24$ students."
